CHECKED AND NOT CHECKED
- Programs run or compiled where a toolchain is on this machine: Python (the split program run under the interpreter, both orders), JavaScript (`node --check`, and the split program loaded as ES modules), Rust (`rustc`, only the missing `extlib` errors), C++ (`g++ -fsyntax-only`, the same), Perl (`perl -c`, and the split program run).
- NOT compiled: TypeScript, Java, Kotlin, Scala, Groovy, C#, Go, Swift, Objective-C, Ruby, PHP, Lua. They were written and read with care; a Scala package named `util` may clash with `scala.util` under a real compiler (that predates this PR).
- The gaps the new cells show (PHP qualified call with no edge; the unresolved qualified calls; C# and Objective-C across files; Groovy with three candidates) are not investigated here and are filed after the merge.
- Swift, decoy last: the decoy class files sort before `Sources/Util/util.swift`; Objective-C, decoy first: `Util.h` / `Util.m` sort before the `a_` files. Neither involves two candidates for one callee.
